7:["$","div",null,{"className":"prose prose-slate max-w-none dark:prose-invert prose-h2:text-2xl prose-h2:tracking-tight prose-p:leading-8 prose-a:text-blue-700","children":[["$","section","Why PDF and image tools belong together",{"className":"mb-10","children":[["$","h2",null,{"children":"Why PDF and image tools belong together"}],[["$","p","PDFs and images frequently appear in the same workflow. A user may extract a PDF page as an image, compress that image, crop it for a support article, convert it to WebP, and then attach it to a page. Another user may combine product images into a PDF catalog or turn scanned pages into image files for review.",{"children":[["$","$1","0",{"children":"PDFs and images frequently appear in the same workflow. A user may extract a PDF page as an image, compress that image, crop it for a support article, convert it to WebP, and then attach it to a page. Another user may combine product images into a PDF catalog or turn scanned pages into image files for review."}]]}],["$","p","Treating these as separate silos creates extra friction. A shared hub helps users move between document and image operations without searching again. It also gives search engines a clearer understanding of ToolOrbit as a practical file utility site.",{"children":[["$","$1","0",{"children":"Treating these as separate silos creates extra friction. A shared hub helps users move between document and image operations without searching again. It also gives search engines a clearer understanding of ToolOrbit as a practical file utility site."}]]}],["$","p","The most important rule is to choose the least destructive operation. Split before merging. Compress a copy, not the only original. Convert formats based on the final use case, not habit.",{"children":[["$","$1","0",{"children":"The most important rule is to choose the least destructive operation. Split before merging. Compress a copy, not the only original. Convert formats based on the final use case, not habit."}]]}],["$","p","A shared hub also reveals natural tool chains that might not be obvious when PDF and image tools live on separate sites. For example, converting a document to images, cropping each page, compressing the crops, and packaging them back into a lean PDF is a common archival workflow that crosses the PDF-image boundary multiple times.",{"children":[["$","$1","0",{"children":"A shared hub also reveals natural tool chains that might not be obvious when PDF and image tools live on separate sites. For example, converting a document to images, cropping each page, compressing the crops, and packaging them back into a lean PDF is a common archival workflow that crosses the PDF-image boundary multiple times."}]]}]]]}],["$","section","How to decide between PDF, PNG, JPEG, WebP, and SVG",{"className":"mb-10","children":[["$","h2",null,{"children":"How to decide between PDF, PNG, JPEG, WebP, and SVG"}],[["$","p","Use PDF when layout preservation matters: contracts, reports, invoices, manuals, or printable documents. Use PNG for transparency, screenshots, and crisp UI captures. Use JPEG for photographic content where small artifacts are acceptable. Use WebP for web delivery when browser support and tooling are available.",{"children":[["$","$1","0",{"children":"Use PDF when layout preservation matters: contracts, reports, invoices, manuals, or printable documents. Use PNG for transparency, screenshots, and crisp UI captures. Use JPEG for photographic content where small artifacts are acceptable. Use WebP for web delivery when browser support and tooling are available."}]]}],"$Lf","$L10","$L11"]]}],"$L12","$L13","$L14","$L15","$L16","$L17"]}]
8:["$","section",null,{"className":"mb-12 border-y border-blue-100 bg-blue-50/40 py-6 dark:border-blue-950 dark:bg-blue-950/20","children":[["$","div",null,{"className":"mb-5 flex items-center gap-3","children":[["$","span",null,{"className":"flex h-9 w-9 items-center justify-center rounded-md bg-blue-600 text-white","children":["$","svg",null,{"xmlns":"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg","width":24,"height":24,"viewBox":"0 0 24 24","fill":"none","stroke":"currentColor","strokeWidth":2,"strokeLinecap":"round","strokeLinejoin":"round","className":"lucide lucide-wrench h-5 w-5","aria-hidden":"true","children":[["$","path","1ngwbx",{"d":"M14.7 6.3a1 1 0 0 0 0 1.4l1.6 1.6a1 1 0 0 0 1.4 0l3.106-3.105c.32-.322.863-.22.983.218a6 6 0 0 1-8.259 7.057l-7.91 7.91a1 1 0 0 1-2.999-3l7.91-7.91a6 6 0 0 1 7.057-8.259c.438.12.54.662.219.984z"}],"$undefined"]}]}],["$","div",null,{"children":[["$","h2",null,{"className":"text-xl font-semibold text-slate-950 dark:text-white","children":"Related ToolOrbit Tools"}],["$","p",null,{"className":"text-sm text-slate-600 dark:text-slate-300","children":"Open the specific utility when you are ready to apply the workflow."}]]}]]}],["$","div",null,{"className":"grid gap-3 sm:grid-cols-2 lg:grid-cols-3","children":[["$","$L18","/tools/pdf/pdf-merge",{"href":"/tools/pdf/pdf-merge","className":"group flex min-h-24 flex-col justify-between rounded-md border border-slate-200 bg-white p-4 shadow-sm transition-colors hover:border-blue-300 hover:bg-blue-50/20 dark:border-slate-800 dark:bg-slate-900 dark:hover:border-blue-700 dark:hover:bg-blue-950/20","children":[["$","span",null,{"className":"font-semibold text-slate-950 group-hover:text-blue-700 dark:text-white dark:group-hover:text-blue-300","children":"PDF Merge"}],["$","span",null,{"className":"mt-2 line-clamp-2 text-sm leading-6 text-slate-600 dark:text-slate-300","children":"Merge multiple PDF files into one."}]]}],["$","$L18","/tools/pdf/pdf-split",{"href":"/tools/pdf/pdf-split","className":"group flex min-h-24 flex-col justify-between rounded-md border border-slate-200 bg-white p-4 shadow-sm transition-colors hover:border-blue-300 hover:bg-blue-50/20 dark:border-slate-800 dark:bg-slate-900 dark:hover:border-blue-700 dark:hover:bg-blue-950/20","children":[["$","span",null,{"className":"font-semibold text-slate-950 group-hover:text-blue-700 dark:text-white dark:group-hover:text-blue-300","children":"PDF Split"}],["$","span",null,{"className":"mt-2 line-clamp-2 text-sm leading-6 text-slate-600 dark:text-slate-300","children":"Split PDF files into multiple parts."}]]}],["$","$L18","/tools/pdf/pdf-to-image",{"href":"/tools/pdf/pdf-to-image","className":"group flex min-h-24 flex-col justify-between rounded-md border border-slate-200 bg-white p-4 shadow-sm transition-colors hover:border-blue-300 hover:bg-blue-50/20 dark:border-slate-800 dark:bg-slate-900 dark:hover:border-blue-700 dark:hover:bg-blue-950/20","children":[["$","span",null,{"className":"font-semibold text-slate-950 group-hover:text-blue-700 dark:text-white dark:group-hover:text-blue-300","children":"PDF to Image"}],["$","span",null,{"className":"mt-2 line-clamp-2 text-sm leading-6 text-slate-600 dark:text-slate-300","children":"Convert PDF pages to JPEG/PNG images."}]]}],["$","$L18","/tools/pdf/image-to-pdf",{"href":"/tools/pdf/image-to-pdf","className":"group flex min-h-24 flex-col justify-between rounded-md border border-slate-200 bg-white p-4 shadow-sm transition-colors hover:border-blue-300 hover:bg-blue-50/20 dark:border-slate-800 dark:bg-slate-900 dark:hover:border-blue-700 dark:hover:bg-blue-950/20","children":[["$","span",null,{"className":"font-semibold text-slate-950 group-hover:text-blue-700 dark:text-white dark:group-hover:text-blue-300","children":"Image to PDF"}],"$L19"]}],"$L1a","$L1b","$L1c","$L1d","$L1e","$L1f","$L20","$L21","$L22","$L23","$L24"]}]]}]
9:["$","section",null,{"className":"mb-12","children":[["$","h2",null,{"className":"mb-5 text-xl font-semibold text-slate-950 dark:text-white","children":"Related Guides"}],["$","div",null,{"className":"grid gap-4 md:grid-cols-2","children":[["$","$L18","modern-pdf-workflow-efficiency",{"href":"/blog/modern-pdf-workflow-efficiency","className":"group rounded-lg border border-slate-200 bg-white p-5 shadow-sm transition-colors hover:border-blue-300 hover:bg-blue-50/20 dark:border-slate-800 dark:bg-slate-900 dark:hover:border-blue-700 dark:hover:bg-blue-950/20","children":[["$","span",null,{"className":"text-xs font-semibold uppercase tracking-wide text-blue-700 dark:text-blue-300","children":"Development"}],["$","h3",null,{"className":"mt-2 text-lg font-semibold text-slate-950 group-hover:text-blue-700 dark:text-white dark:group-hover:text-blue-300","children":"Modern PDF Workflows: Boosting Efficiency with Merge, Split, and Encryption"}],["$","p",null,{"className":"mt-2 line-clamp-2 text-sm leading-6 text-slate-600 dark:text-slate-300","children":"PDF is a cornerstone of business. Learn how to optimize your PDF process using modern tools to ensure security and speed."}],["$","span",null,{"className":"mt-4 inline-flex items-center gap-2 text-sm font-semibold text-blue-700 dark:text-blue-300","children":["Read guide"," ",["$","svg",null,{"xmlns":"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg","width":24,"height":24,"viewBox":"0 0 24 24","fill":"none","stroke":"currentColor","strokeWidth":2,"strokeLinecap":"round","strokeLinejoin":"round","className":"lucide lucide-arrow-right h-4 w-4","aria-hidden":"true","children":[["$","path","1ays0h",{"d":"M5 12h14"}],["$","path","xquz4c",{"d":"m12 5 7 7-7 7"}],"$undefined"]}]]}]]}],["$","$L18","image-compression-techniques",{"href":"/blog/image-compression-techniques","className":"group rounded-lg border border-slate-200 bg-white p-5 shadow-sm transition-colors hover:border-blue-300 hover:bg-blue-50/20 dark:border-slate-800 dark:bg-slate-900 dark:hover:border-blue-700 dark:hover:bg-blue-950/20","children":[["$","span",null,{"className":"text-xs font-semibold uppercase tracking-wide text-blue-700 dark:text-blue-300","children":"Design"}],["$","h3",null,{"className":"mt-2 text-lg font-semibold text-slate-950 group-hover:text-blue-700 dark:text-white dark:group-hover:text-blue-300","children":"Mastering Image Compression: Speed Up Your Website Without Losing Quality"}],["$","p",null,{"className":"mt-2 line-clamp-2 text-sm leading-6 text-slate-600 dark:text-slate-300","children":"Large images are the enemy of fast websites. Learn how to effectively compress images to boost your site's performance and SEO."}],["$","span",null,{"className":"mt-4 inline-flex items-center gap-2 text-sm font-semibold text-blue-700 dark:text-blue-300","children":["Read guide"," ",["$","svg",null,{"xmlns":"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg","width":24,"height":24,"viewBox":"0 0 24 24","fill":"none","stroke":"currentColor","strokeWidth":2,"strokeLinecap":"round","strokeLinejoin":"round","className":"lucide lucide-arrow-right h-4 w-4","aria-hidden":"true","children":[["$","path","1ays0h",{"d":"M5 12h14"}],["$","path","xquz4c",{"d":"m12 5 7 7-7 7"}],"$undefined"]}]]}]]}],["$","$L18","url-encoding-demystified",{"href":"/blog/url-encoding-demystified","className":"group rounded-lg border border-slate-200 bg-white p-5 shadow-sm transition-colors hover:border-blue-300 hover:bg-blue-50/20 dark:border-slate-800 dark:bg-slate-900 dark:hover:border-blue-700 dark:hover:bg-blue-950/20","children":[["$","span",null,{"className":"text-xs font-semibold uppercase tracking-wide text-blue-700 dark:text-blue-300","children":"Development"}],["$","h3",null,{"className":"mt-2 text-lg font-semibold text-slate-950 group-hover:text-blue-700 dark:text-white dark:group-hover:text-blue-300","children":"URL Encoding Demystified: Safe Characters, Query Strings, and Browser Behavior"}],"$L25","$L26"]}],"$L27","$L28","$L29","$L2a"]}]]}]
a:["$","section",null,{"className":"mb-12","children":[["$","h2",null,{"className":"mb-5 text-xl font-semibold text-slate-950 dark:text-white","children":"FAQ"}],["$","div",null,{"className":"space-y-3","children":[["$","details","Can browser PDF tools handle private documents?",{"className":"border-b border-slate-200 py-4 dark:border-slate-800","children":[["$","summary",null,{"className":"cursor-pointer text-base font-semibold text-slate-950 dark:text-white","children":"Can browser PDF tools handle private documents?"}],["$","p",null,{"className":"mt-3 leading-7 text-slate-700 dark:text-slate-300","children":"They are preferable when the operation runs locally in the browser. Users should still avoid uploading confidential documents to unknown services and should verify each tool network behavior via browser DevTools."}]]}],["$","details","What is the best image format for websites?",{"className":"border-b border-slate-200 py-4 dark:border-slate-800","children":[["$","summary",null,{"className":"cursor-pointer text-base font-semibold text-slate-950 dark:text-white","children":"What is the best image format for websites?"}],["$","p",null,{"className":"mt-3 leading-7 text-slate-700 dark:text-slate-300","children":"WebP is a practical default for many web images, SVG is best for vector graphics, PNG is best for transparency and screenshots, and JPEG remains useful for photos when compatibility matters. The best format is the one that minimizes file size without degrading perceived quality for the specific content type."}]]}],["$","details","Should I compress images before or after cropping?",{"className":"border-b border-slate-200 py-4 dark:border-slate-800","children":[["$","summary",null,{"className":"cursor-pointer text-base font-semibold text-slate-950 dark:text-white","children":"Should I compress images before or after cropping?"}],["$","p",null,{"className":"mt-3 leading-7 text-slate-700 dark:text-slate-300","children":"Crop and resize first, then compress. Removing unnecessary pixels before compression usually produces better results with smaller file sizes."}]]}],["$","details","Can I merge PDFs of different page sizes?",{"className":"border-b border-slate-200 py-4 dark:border-slate-800","children":[["$","summary",null,{"className":"cursor-pointer text-base font-semibold text-slate-950 dark:text-white","children":"Can I merge PDFs of different page sizes?"}],["$","p",null,{"className":"mt-3 leading-7 text-slate-700 dark:text-slate-300","children":"Yes, but check the output carefully. Mixing A4 and Letter pages, or portrait and landscape orientations, can produce awkward results. Standardize page sizes and orientations before merging when possible."}]]}],["$","details","Why does my SVG look different after converting to PNG?",{"className":"border-b border-slate-200 py-4 dark:border-slate-800","children":[["$","summary",null,{"className":"cursor-pointer text-base font-semibold text-slate-950 dark:text-white","children":"Why does my SVG look different after converting to PNG?"}],["$","p",null,{"className":"mt-3 leading-7 text-slate-700 dark:text-slate-300","children":"SVG rendering depends on the rendering engine, and fonts, filters, and complex gradients may not translate perfectly. Convert at a high resolution, check the output, and simplify complex SVGs before conversion when fidelity matters."}]]}],["$","details","Is Base64 embedding better than linking image files?",{"className":"border-b border-slate-200 py-4 dark:border-slate-800","children":[["$","summary",null,{"className":"cursor-pointer text-base font-semibold text-slate-950 dark:text-white","children":"Is Base64 embedding better than linking image files?"}],"$L2b"]}]]}]]}]
b:["$","footer",null,{"className":"border-t border-slate-200 pt-5 text-sm leading-6 text-slate-600 dark:border-slate-800 dark:text-slate-300","children":[["$","p",null,{"className":"flex items-start gap-2","children":[["$","svg",null,{"xmlns":"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg","width":24,"height":24,"viewBox":"0 0 24 24","fill":"none","stroke":"currentColor","strokeWidth":2,"strokeLinecap":"round","strokeLinejoin":"round","className":"lucide lucide-circle-check mt-0.5 h-4 w-4 shrink-0 text-blue-600","aria-hidden":"true","children":[["$","circle","1mglay",{"cx":"12","cy":"12","r":"10"}],["$","path","dzmm74",{"d":"m9 12 2 2 4-4"}],"$undefined"]}],"Maintained by the ToolOrbit Editorial Team. This page links to practical tools and supporting guides so readers can verify the workflow rather than relying on broad claims."]}],["$","$L18",null,{"href":"/authors/toolorbit-editorial-team","className":"mt-3 inline-flex items-center gap-2 font-semibold text-blue-700 dark:text-blue-300","children":["Editorial team profile"," ",["$","svg",null,{"xmlns":"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg","width":24,"height":24,"viewBox":"0 0 24 24","fill":"none","stroke":"currentColor","strokeWidth":2,"strokeLinecap":"round","strokeLinejoin":"round","className":"lucide lucide-external-link h-4 w-4","aria-hidden":"true","children":[["$","path","1q9fwt",{"d":"M15 3h6v6"}],["$","path","gplh6r",{"d":"M10 14 21 3"}],["$","path","a6xqqp",{"d":"M18 13v6a2 2 0 0 1-2 2H5a2 2 0 0 1-2-2V8a2 2 0 0 1 2-2h6"}],"$undefined"]}]]}]]}]
e:null
f:["$","p","Use SVG for logos, icons, diagrams, and simple illustrations that should stay sharp at every size. Convert SVG to PNG only when a platform does not support SVG or when you need a raster export for sharing.",{"children":[["$","$1","0",{"children":"Use SVG for logos, icons, diagrams, and simple illustrations that should stay sharp at every size. Convert SVG to PNG only when a platform does not support SVG or when you need a raster export for sharing."}]]}]
10:["$","p","For SEO and performance, the best image is not just the smallest file. It is the smallest file that preserves user confidence, includes stable dimensions, and does not delay the main content of the page.",{"children":[["$","$1","0",{"children":"For SEO and performance, the best image is not just the smallest file. It is the smallest file that preserves user confidence, includes stable dimensions, and does not delay the main content of the page."}]]}]
11:["$","p","A practical decision framework: if it has text or sharp lines, prefer PNG or SVG. If it is a photograph, JPEG or WebP. If it will be printed, PDF or high-resolution PNG. If it will be embedded in a webpage, WebP with a JPEG fallback. If it is an icon or logo that should scale infinitely, SVG. When in doubt, keep the original and test the converted version side by side.",{"children":[["$","$1","0",{"children":"A practical decision framework: if it has text or sharp lines, prefer PNG or SVG. If it is a photograph, JPEG or WebP. If it will be printed, PDF or high-resolution PNG. If it will be embedded in a webpage, WebP with a JPEG fallback. If it is an icon or logo that should scale infinitely, SVG. When in doubt, keep the original and test the converted version side by side."}]]}]
12:["$","section","A practical file workflow for teams",{"className":"mb-10","children":[["$","h2",null,{"children":"A practical file workflow for teams"}],[["$","p","Start by deciding whether the result is for reading, printing, uploading, or publishing on the web. If the goal is reading or printing, PDF tools usually come first. If the goal is publishing, image compression, cropping, and format conversion matter more.",{"children":[["$","$1","0",{"children":"Start by deciding whether the result is for reading, printing, uploading, or publishing on the web. If the goal is reading or printing, PDF tools usually come first. If the goal is publishing, image compression, cropping, and format conversion matter more."}]]}],["$","p","Next, remove unnecessary pages or pixels. Split a PDF before sharing a small excerpt. Crop a screenshot before compressing it. Convert a full-size photo only after you know the required dimensions. This reduces file size while keeping quality decisions intentional.",{"children":[["$","$1","0",{"children":"Next, remove unnecessary pages or pixels. Split a PDF before sharing a small excerpt. Crop a screenshot before compressing it. Convert a full-size photo only after you know the required dimensions. This reduces file size while keeping quality decisions intentional."}]]}],["$","p","Finally, verify the result. Open merged PDFs, inspect image edges, check transparency, and confirm that file size actually improved. ToolOrbit keeps these checks close to the tools so users can iterate quickly.",{"children":[["$","$1","0",{"children":"Finally, verify the result. Open merged PDFs, inspect image edges, check transparency, and confirm that file size actually improved. ToolOrbit keeps these checks close to the tools so users can iterate quickly."}]]}],["$","p","For teams, standardize the workflow. Agree on target formats, maximum file sizes, and naming conventions. Document the sequence in a shared playbook. When every team member follows the same optimization path, the site stays fast, the documents stay consistent, and the support queue sees fewer formatting-related tickets.",{"children":[["$","$1","0",{"children":"For teams, standardize the workflow. Agree on target formats, maximum file sizes, and naming conventions. Document the sequence in a shared playbook. When every team member follows the same optimization path, the site stays fast, the documents stay consistent, and the support queue sees fewer formatting-related tickets."}]]}]]]}]
13:["$","section","PDF merge and split: getting predictable results",{"className":"mb-10","children":[["$","h2",null,{"children":"PDF merge and split: getting predictable results"}],[["$","p","PDF merge is deceptively simple. Combine the wrong pages, merge files with different page orientations, or introduce a corrupted source PDF, and the output is broken. The most reliable approach is to verify each source PDF before merging: open it, confirm the page count, and check that pages are oriented correctly.",{"children":[["$","$1","0",{"children":"PDF merge is deceptively simple. Combine the wrong pages, merge files with different page orientations, or introduce a corrupted source PDF, and the output is broken. The most reliable approach is to verify each source PDF before merging: open it, confirm the page count, and check that pages are oriented correctly."}]]}],["$","p","When merging, order matters. A contract followed by an appendix is a clean document. A random page inserted in the middle is a support ticket. Arrange source PDFs in the intended reading order before starting the merge operation.",{"children":[["$","$1","0",{"children":"When merging, order matters. A contract followed by an appendix is a clean document. A random page inserted in the middle is a support ticket. Arrange source PDFs in the intended reading order before starting the merge operation."}]]}],["$","p","PDF split is the safer operation and should be preferred when you only need a subset of pages. Extract the pages you need, verify them, and share only those. This reduces file size, removes irrelevant content, and makes the document easier for recipients to navigate.",{"children":[["$","$1","0",{"children":"PDF split is the safer operation and should be preferred when you only need a subset of pages. Extract the pages you need, verify them, and share only those. This reduces file size, removes irrelevant content, and makes the document easier for recipients to navigate."}]]}],["$","p","For both operations, always open the output PDF after processing. Confirm page count, orientation, and that embedded images and text remain intact. A five-second visual check prevents a re-send and an apology email.",{"children":[["$","$1","0",{"children":"For both operations, always open the output PDF after processing. Confirm page count, orientation, and that embedded images and text remain intact. A five-second visual check prevents a re-send and an apology email."}]]}]]]}]
14:["$","section","Image compression: quality, speed, and SEO",{"className":"mb-10","children":[["$","h2",null,{"children":"Image compression: quality, speed, and SEO"}],[["$","p","Image compression is one of the highest-ROI performance optimizations a site owner can make. A single uncompressed screenshot can be 2 MB. Compressed to WebP at reasonable quality, it might be 80 KB. Multiply that across a blog post with ten images, and the page weight drops from 20 MB to under 1 MB.",{"children":[["$","$1","0",{"children":"Image compression is one of the highest-ROI performance optimizations a site owner can make. A single uncompressed screenshot can be 2 MB. Compressed to WebP at reasonable quality, it might be 80 KB. Multiply that across a blog post with ten images, and the page weight drops from 20 MB to under 1 MB."}]]}],["$","p","The art of compression is finding the quality threshold where the image still looks professional but the file size is substantially reduced. For screenshots and UI captures, aggressive compression often works because the content is mostly flat color and sharp edges. For photographs, gentler compression preserves gradients and subtle detail.",{"children":[["$","$1","0",{"children":"The art of compression is finding the quality threshold where the image still looks professional but the file size is substantially reduced. For screenshots and UI captures, aggressive compression often works because the content is mostly flat color and sharp edges. For photographs, gentler compression preserves gradients and subtle detail."}]]}],["$","p","Always compress a copy, not the original. Keep the original at full resolution for future edits, and produce compressed versions at the exact dimensions needed for the target layout. This is especially important for ecommerce product images, where you may need the original for a zoom feature and compressed versions for thumbnails and gallery views.",{"children":[["$","$1","0",{"children":"Always compress a copy, not the original. Keep the original at full resolution for future edits, and produce compressed versions at the exact dimensions needed for the target layout. This is especially important for ecommerce product images, where you may need the original for a zoom feature and compressed versions for thumbnails and gallery views."}]]}],["$","p","For SEO, compressed images improve Core Web Vitals directly. Largest Contentful Paint (LCP) often depends on hero image load time. Cumulative Layout Shift (CLS) is reduced when images have explicit width and height attributes. Neither of these is the compressor job, but both depend on having properly sized, efficiently encoded image files.",{"children":[["$","$1","0",{"children":"For SEO, compressed images improve Core Web Vitals directly. Largest Contentful Paint (LCP) often depends on hero image load time. Cumulative Layout Shift (CLS) is reduced when images have explicit width and height attributes. Neither of these is the compressor job, but both depend on having properly sized, efficiently encoded image files."}]]}]]]}]
15:["$","section","SVG to PNG: when vectors need to become rasters",{"className":"mb-10","children":[["$","h2",null,{"children":"SVG to PNG: when vectors need to become rasters"}],[["$","p","SVG is the ideal format for logos, icons, diagrams, and illustrations. It scales infinitely, has tiny file sizes, and can be styled with CSS. But not every platform accepts SVG. Email clients, some social media platforms, certain CMS upload fields, and older document processors require raster formats.",{"children":[["$","$1","0",{"children":"SVG is the ideal format for logos, icons, diagrams, and illustrations. It scales infinitely, has tiny file sizes, and can be styled with CSS. But not every platform accepts SVG. Email clients, some social media platforms, certain CMS upload fields, and older document processors require raster formats."}]]}],["$","p","When converting SVG to PNG, the critical decision is resolution. Convert at the largest size you will need, then scale down as necessary. It is always possible to reduce a PNG dimensions; it is not possible to add detail that was never rendered. For logos destined for both a website header and a print brochure, generate the print-resolution PNG first and downscale for the web.",{"children":[["$","$1","0",{"children":"When converting SVG to PNG, the critical decision is resolution. Convert at the largest size you will need, then scale down as necessary. It is always possible to reduce a PNG dimensions; it is not possible to add detail that was never rendered. For logos destined for both a website header and a print brochure, generate the print-resolution PNG first and downscale for the web."}]]}],["$","p","Pay attention to transparency. Many SVGs use transparent backgrounds, and the resulting PNG should preserve that transparency. A logo with a white background baked in is less useful than one with a transparent background. Check the output against both light and dark backgrounds before finalizing.",{"children":[["$","$1","0",{"children":"Pay attention to transparency. Many SVGs use transparent backgrounds, and the resulting PNG should preserve that transparency. A logo with a white background baked in is less useful than one with a transparent background. Check the output against both light and dark backgrounds before finalizing."}]]}],["$","p","For developers, SVG-to-PNG conversion is also useful for generating favicon sets. Start with a clean SVG icon, export at 16x16, 32x32, 48x48, 96x96, and 180x180, and you have a complete favicon package without needing a graphic design tool.",{"children":[["$","$1","0",{"children":"For developers, SVG-to-PNG conversion is also useful for generating favicon sets. Start with a clean SVG icon, export at 16x16, 32x32, 48x48, 96x96, and 180x180, and you have a complete favicon package without needing a graphic design tool."}]]}]]]}]
16:["$","section","Why local-first file utilities are a trust signal",{"className":"mb-10","children":[["$","h2",null,{"children":"Why local-first file utilities are a trust signal"}],[["$","p","File utilities often handle sensitive documents. A browser-based local workflow can reduce unnecessary uploads, which matters for contracts, invoices, internal screenshots, and unpublished creative work.",{"children":[["$","$1","0",{"children":"File utilities often handle sensitive documents. A browser-based local workflow can reduce unnecessary uploads, which matters for contracts, invoices, internal screenshots, and unpublished creative work."}]]}],["$","p","That trust signal also supports SEO. Pages that clearly explain privacy, workflow, and use cases are more useful than thin upload boxes. This hub links to both tools and explanatory guides so users can understand what to use and why.",{"children":[["$","$1","0",{"children":"That trust signal also supports SEO. Pages that clearly explain privacy, workflow, and use cases are more useful than thin upload boxes. This hub links to both tools and explanatory guides so users can understand what to use and why."}]]}],["$","p","The privacy advantage of local-first file tools is not just about security. It is also about speed and control. A local merge or compression completes immediately, without waiting for an upload queue. The user can iterate quickly, comparing different compression levels or merge orders without each attempt incurring a round-trip to a remote server.",{"children":[["$","$1","0",{"children":"The privacy advantage of local-first file tools is not just about security. It is also about speed and control. A local merge or compression completes immediately, without waiting for an upload queue. The user can iterate quickly, comparing different compression levels or merge orders without each attempt incurring a round-trip to a remote server."}]]}],["$","p","For organizations with data residency requirements, local-first tools eliminate the question of where the file was processed. If the PDF never left the browser, it never left the jurisdiction. That is a simpler answer than reviewing the data processing agreement of every cloud-based file utility.",{"children":[["$","$1","0",{"children":"For organizations with data residency requirements, local-first tools eliminate the question of where the file was processed. If the PDF never left the browser, it never left the jurisdiction. That is a simpler answer than reviewing the data processing agreement of every cloud-based file utility."}]]}]]]}]
17:["$","section","Common file mistakes and how to avoid them",{"className":"mb-10","children":[["$","h2",null,{"children":"Common file mistakes and how to avoid them"}],[["$","p","The most common PDF mistake is sharing a file that is far larger than necessary. High-resolution scans, embedded fonts, and uncompressed images can bloat a PDF to tens of megabytes. Before sharing, check the file size. If it seems large, consider extracting only the needed pages or compressing embedded images.",{"children":[["$","$1","0",{"children":"The most common PDF mistake is sharing a file that is far larger than necessary. High-resolution scans, embedded fonts, and uncompressed images can bloat a PDF to tens of megabytes. Before sharing, check the file size. If it seems large, consider extracting only the needed pages or compressing embedded images."}]]}],["$","p","The most common image mistake for the web is uploading a full-resolution photo and letting CSS resize it. A 4000-pixel-wide photo displayed at 800 pixels still downloads all 4000 pixels. Crop and resize to the display dimensions before uploading. The browser should not be your image resizer.",{"children":[["$","$1","0",{"children":"The most common image mistake for the web is uploading a full-resolution photo and letting CSS resize it. A 4000-pixel-wide photo displayed at 800 pixels still downloads all 4000 pixels. Crop and resize to the display dimensions before uploading. The browser should not be your image resizer."}]]}],["$","p","The most common format mistake is using the wrong format for the content. A photograph saved as PNG is often 5-10x larger than the same image as JPEG. A screenshot saved as JPEG often looks worse than the same image as PNG. Format selection is not aesthetic; it is driven by the content type and the compression characteristics of each format.",{"children":[["$","$1","0",{"children":"The most common format mistake is using the wrong format for the content. A photograph saved as PNG is often 5-10x larger than the same image as JPEG. A screenshot saved as JPEG often looks worse than the same image as PNG. Format selection is not aesthetic; it is driven by the content type and the compression characteristics of each format."}]]}],["$","p","The most common workflow mistake is operating on the only copy of a file. Always keep the original. Work on a duplicate. Verify the output before deleting anything. This rule applies whether you are merging PDFs, compressing images, converting formats, or cropping screenshots. Storage is cheap; recreating lost content is not.",{"children":[["$","$1","0",{"children":"The most common workflow mistake is operating on the only copy of a file. Always keep the original. Work on a duplicate. Verify the output before deleting anything. This rule applies whether you are merging PDFs, compressing images, converting formats, or cropping screenshots. Storage is cheap; recreating lost content is not."}]]}]]]}]
